{"entities":[{"text":"Ethacrynic acid-induced","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"ethacrynic acid","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"5-hydroxytryptamine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"5-HT","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"acetylcholine","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"glutamate","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"ethacrynic acid-induced","label":"Chemical","id":""},{"text":"convulsions","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"convulsive","label":"Disease","id":""},{"text":"convulsions","label":"Disease","id":""}],"entity_aliases":[{"text":"Ethacrynic acid","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"ethacrynic acid","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"5-HT","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"5-hydroxytryptamine","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"acetylcholine","id":"4","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"glutamate","id":"5","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","id":"6","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","id":"7","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"convulsive","id":"1","label":"Disease"},{"text":"convulsions","id":"1","label":"Disease"}],"filtered_entities":[{"text":"Ethacrynic acid","id":"1","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"5-hydroxytryptamine","id":"2","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","id":"3","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"acetylcholine","id":"4","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"glutamate","id":"5","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","id":"6","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","id":"7","label":"Chemical"},{"text":"convulsions","id":"1","label":"Disease"}],"gold_relations":"ethacrynic acid | CID | convulsions","labels":"Chemical,Disease","metrics":{"precision":1.0,"recall":1.0,"f1":1.0,"rel_tp":1,"rel_fp":0,"rel_fn":0},"pairs":[{"head":"Ethacrynic acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"1","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"5-hydroxytryptamine","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"2","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"gamma-aminobutyric acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"3","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"acetylcholine","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"4","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"glutamate","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"5","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"N-methyl-D-aspartate","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"6","tail_id":"1"},{"head":"aminophosphonovaleric acid","tail":"convulsions","head_id":"7","tail_id":"1"}],"relations":["1 | 1"],"text":"Ethacrynic acid-induced convulsions and brain neurotransmitters in mice. Intracerebroventricular injection of ethacrynic acid (50% convulsive dose; 50 micrograms/mouse) accelerated the synthesis/turnover of 5-hydroxytryptamine (5-HT) but suppressed the synthesis of gamma-aminobutyric acid and acetylcholine in mouse brain. These effects were completely antagonized by pretreatment with a glutamate/N-methyl-D-aspartate antagonist, aminophosphonovaleric acid. In ethacrynic acid-induced convulsions, these neurotransmitter systems may be differentially modulated, probably through activation of glutaminergic neurons in the brain."}